  <tei:standOff type="notes">
    <tei:note type="commentary" target="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:torah_tziva/morasha">
      <tei:p><tei:label xml:lang="he">תורה צוה לנו</tei:label> (Deuteronomy 33:4) is the first Hebrew verse which a father is directed to teach his child at a very early age (Sukkah 42a; Maimonides, <tei:hi rend="italic">Talmud Torah</tei:hi> 1:6). Although the child is held to be free from religious duties, his father is required to make him amenable to them.</tei:p>
    </tei:note>
